   - 35 clusters with X-ray temperatures and baryonic masses
   - Sources: Vikhlinin+2006 (10 clusters), CLASH (25 clusters)
   - Fits: BTFR scaling relation (sigma^4 = a0 × G × M_bar)
   - Computes: Mean & Median residuals, BTFR slope, R²

ALL RESULTS ARE COMPUTED LIVE — NOTHING IS HARDCODED.

================================================================================
RESIDUAL DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

SPARC Residual: Mean/Median absolute percent difference between predicted and
observed rotation velocities across ALL radial points in each galaxy.
Individual galaxy residual: 100 * |V_pred(r) - V_obs(r)| / V_obs(r)

MaNGA Residual: Mean/Median absolute percent difference between predicted and
observed V_flat at r_max.
Individual galaxy residual: 100 * |V_pred - V_flat| / V_flat
where V_pred = V_flat × (1 - exp(-r_max / r_t))

Clusters Residual: Mean/Median absolute percent difference between predicted and
observed velocity dispersion.
Individual cluster residual: 100 * |sigma_pred - sigma_obs| / sigma_obs
where sigma_pred = (a0 × G × M_bar)^(1/4)

================================================================================
